The bug was an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was returning `parts[1]` (the second word) instead of `parts[0]` (the first word). This caused:
- `first_word('hello world')` to return `'world'` instead of `'hello'`
- `first_word('solo')` to crash with an IndexError since there's only one element at index 0

The fix was simple: change `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]`.
